{
  "version": "1.3",
  "naming_set": "chemist_style",
  "notes": [
    "Chemist-facing compound motifs derived from organic_groups via simple connection templates.",
    "A/B are group IDs from organic_groups.v1.json; template is a key in smarts_templates.v1.json.",
    "Entries prefixed with 'Any-' use A='R' (generic attachment) to indicate a global functional-group presence without specifying alkyl vs aryl.",
    "v1.1: added R–X (alkyl halides), R–OTf/OTs/OMs (alkyl sulfonates), and terminal alkyne/alkene motifs to support Sonogashira/Heck/SN2 typing.",
    "v1.2: no motif list changes; this version pairs with organic_groups.v1.2 tags to auto-generate reaction roles.",
    "v1.3: added standardized anchors for each compound entry to support runtime calculators/term-tags. anchors.core = attachment atom on A-side (core scaffold); anchors.fg = attachment atom on B-side (functional group / leaving group)."
  ],
